      "raw_text": "71   Bt pesticide is used by farmers to kill insect pests. However, widespread use has resulted in\n     the evolution of resistance to this pesticide. A recessive allele causes resistance.\n     Scientists have suggested that in areas where the Bt pesticide is used, a small number of fields\n     are left untreated. These untreated fields are known as refugia. This method has been shown\n     to slow down evolution of resistance to the pesticide.\n     Which of the following statements explain why refugia could slow down the evolution of\n     resistance to Bt pesticide?\n          1    When resistant insects breed with pesticide-sensitive insects that do not have the\n               allele for resistance, the offspring produced will be sensitive to the pesticide.\n          2    When fewer insects are exposed to pesticide, fewer mutations occur that produce\n               alleles for resistance.\n          3    The refugia help to maintain genetic variation in the population of insect pests.\n     A   none of them\n     B   1 only\n     C   2 only\n     D   3 only\n     E   1 and 2 only\n     F   1 and 3 only\n     G   2 and 3 only\n     H   1, 2 and 3\n                                                 65\n\f                                                                                     PART D Biology",
